## Gate vocabulary

- SOURCE GO binds only the named source bytes and source checks.
- PACKAGE GO binds one immutable, allowlisted package to accepted source. A package does not authorize installation or deployment.
- INSTALLED GO requires exact installed-byte identity and real target-runtime checks.
- DEPLOYMENT GO requires a target-bound single-use activation, sanitized receipt, and appropriate rollback/containment proof.
- LIVE GO requires exact deployed revision or byte proof plus the named behavioral checks.
- COMMIT, PUSH, SIGNING, DESIGN acceptance, and RELEASE acceptance are separate gates. None silently upgrades another.
- Never inherit a stronger gate from an older report, another commit, a synthetic fixture, a debug artifact, or another product.

